entry.summary:
A single model can be unavailable, rate-limited, or temporarily slow. If your application already uses an OpenAI-compatible API, a simple fallback can make testing more resilient without introducing another SDK. This tutorial uses Node.js and the official OpenAI JavaScript package. It tries one model first and switches to a second model only when the first request fails. npm install openai
On macOS or Linux: export JINZEAI_API_KEY="your_api_key_here"
On PowerShell: $env:JINZEAI_API_KEY="your_api_key_here"
Never commit a real API key. Rotate it immediately if it appears in a public repository, screenshot, or support message. import OpenAI from "openai";
const client = new OpenAI({ baseURL: "https://jinzeai.cc/v1", apiKey: process.env.JINZEAI_API_KEY, });
const models = ["deepseek-c…

Hoisting in JavaScript is the engine’s behavior of moving declarations to the top of their scope (global or local) before execution. Because of hoisting, you can reference functions or variables in your code before the lines where they are defined.
1.Function Declaration
hello(); //Output: hello!
function hello(){
   console.log("hello!")
}

2.var Declaration
console.log(num); //Output: undefined
var num = 10;
console.log(num); //Output: 10
